/**
 * Machine-readable reason of onboard_error. Clients localize by reason, never by message text.
 * Waiting device side (every app platform: iPhone, iPad, Apple TV, Apple Watch through its iPhone
 * and the Android counterparts): invalid_request = public_key/client_name missing or malformed;
 * invalid_client_info = malformed client info; platform_not_supported = this client cannot be set
 * up by another device (web); tls_required = onboard_start over the cleartext port (TLS :8100 with
 * the pinned fingerprint is mandatory); rate_limited = start limit of this source IP reached;
 * already_authenticated = the connection is already authenticated; connection_expired = the
 * connection was evicted; session_expired = the 5-minute window has passed (the hub closes 4002
 * right after); session_invalidated = a confirmation carried another public key or hub id than the
 * session (possible man in the middle), the session is gone; declined = the confirming device
 * declined; cancelled = an admin cancelled the session. Confirming device side additionally:
 * session_not_found = unknown, used, expired or cancelled session id or code (“Code not found”);
 * hub_mismatch = the QR code belongs to another hub; not_permitted = this device may not set up
 * devices (effective rule setup_devices off: guests, parental controls, a profile that is not of
 * kind person, or not allowed by profile or adjustment; a watch additionally needs the rule
 * watch); too_many_attempts = too many wrong codes from this device or on the hub (x-limits
 * onboard_code_*; scan the QR code or wait); rate_limited = failure limit of this device reached;
 * kind_not_allowed = the kind is not in setup_devices.kinds of this device or does not fit the
 * platform of the waiting device (also in onboard_lookup when no allowed kind fits it);
 * profile_not_allowed = the profile is not offered for this kind (onboard_info.grant): unknown,
 * another kind, stronger than the rights of the confirming device, or not allowed on the platform
 * of the new device (docs/setup.md, Platform of the profile); areas_not_allowed = the area choice
 * is empty, names an unknown or inactive area, an area the confirming device does not see itself,
 * or all_areas although the confirming device does not see all areas; also an own_area_id or
 * start_area outside grant.areas; expiry_not_allowed = a guest, house sitter or babysitter without
 * expires_at, in the past or more than 90 days ahead (guest_access.max_hours), or an expiry for
 * another kind; managers_not_allowed = managers sent without the right family_manager, or a device
 * that is no family manager; access_hours_not_allowed = access_windows sent although the grant
 * does not offer access hours for the profile (access_hours_choice false: the profile fixes the
 * rule access_hours); device_not_found = set_up_device_remove names no active device set up by
 * this device. Validation errors of onboard_confirm (kind_not_allowed, profile_not_allowed,
 * areas_not_allowed, expiry_not_allowed, managers_not_allowed, access_hours_not_allowed) keep the
 * session open and count as a failed attempt. Clients must treat an unknown reason like
 * session_not_found (show a new code / scan again).
 */
