/**
 * An unpaired device asks for a one-time onboarding session (unauthenticated sessions only, TLS
 * port only): every app platform (ios, ipados, tvos, android, android_tablet, android_tv; a watch
 * (watchos, wearos) through its phone, which opens the session on the watch's behalf with the
 * watch's public key, confirms it itself and passes the sealed secret on to the watch; the watch
 * keeps that key, the hub keeps its public key to seal the watch's HA access to it, watch_access);
 * web gets onboard_error platform_not_supported. The PIN stays available on every device. It sends
 * its ephemeral X25519 public key and the client info like pair (checked first: a too old app gets
 * upgrade_required + close 4426). Answer: onboard_session (with QR data and the 6-digit code), or
 * onboard_error. A second onboard_start on the same connection replaces the running session (new
 * QR code and code). The connection stays open until the session ends (instead of the 30 s auth
