/**
 * Scenes and scripts switch other entities as the system. Running one (an action listed in
 * domains) is allowed only when, besides its own checks and its release, every target is allowed
 * for the device on its own (contract docs/enforcement.md §2 step 4): in the device's snapshot
 * entities, its domain in the allowlist (domains), the level on the route (judged as an unsafe
 * action, except a scene target stored in the safe direction: lock locked, alarm armed), the quick
 * level for origin quick_access, not an entity of the <ns> integration, scenes and scripts among
 * the targets released and checked in turn, and the kids rules of the target (entry, blocked,
 * bedtime, and for scenes color lock and volume cap of the stored state). A failing target refuses
 * the scene or script with blocked_group_member, or with the target's own reason when it is
 * blocked_remote, blocked_quick_access or one of blocked_kids*. Targets of a Home Assistant scene:
 * the entities of its configuration (state attribute entity_id); of a script: the entities Home
