    /**
     * Kind of the device's profile.
     */
    @SerialName("profile_kind") val profileKind: ProfileKind,
    /**
     * true = the device holds a Home Assistant key that Home Assistant still accepts: a delivered key
     * (its effective control_path is checked or direct, or hub with effective remote access: a
     * read-only key), or a withdrawn key whose replacement the integration has not confirmed yet (the
     * old token stays valid until then). false = the device holds none (Hub only without remote
     * access, or a withdrawn key after the integration confirmed the rotation). When a device stops
     * holding a key (control_path becomes hub, remote access ends on Hub only; log entry
     * ha_key_withdrawn; at guest expiry the hub removes the device and its Home Assistant user
     * instead) and when its access closes, the hub rotates the token, so a key the app held before
     * stops working as soon as the integration has removed it (until then it keeps working, and the
     * hub keeps trying). Whether the HA user is set up at all is ha_token_status.
     */
    @SerialName("has_ha_token") val hasHaToken: StrictBoolean,
    /**
     * Effective Home Assistant access of the device (rule control_path after the platform mapping: on
     * tvos, android_tv, watchos and wearos hub is checked). hub = no key unless remote access gives a
     * read-only one (has_ha_token), checked = read-only key, direct = full key. null = the hub could
     * not resolve the device's rules (the cause is in the hub's log; remote_allowed is null too): the
     * key state is unknown, and has_ha_token then only says whether a token exists at all. Missing on
     * older hubs.
     */
    @SerialName("control_path") val controlPath: ControlPathRule? = null,
    @SerialName("owner_label") val ownerLabel: String?,
    @SerialName("profile_id") val profileId: String,
    @SerialName("profile_name") val profileName: String,
    /**
     * Parental controls of the profile (kids rules enforced by the hub and the integration; whether
     * the device holds a Home Assistant key is set by the rule control_path, has_ha_token).
     */
    @SerialName("child_protection") val childProtection: StrictBoolean,
    @SerialName("own_area_id") val ownAreaId: String?,
    @SerialName("override_count") val overrideCount: StrictLong,
    @SerialName("temporary_override_count") val temporaryOverrideCount: StrictLong,
    @SerialName("has_remote_pin") val hasRemotePin: StrictBoolean,
    /**
     * Effective rule remote_access (read only; changed through the profile or an adjustment). The HA
     * user of the device is local_only exactly when this is false. null = the device's rules could not
     * be resolved: only together with control_path null; then access, remote access and key level are
     * unknown.
     */
    @SerialName("remote_allowed") val remoteAllowed: StrictBoolean?,
    /**
     * HA user of this device (set by the integration); null while pending.
     */
    @SerialName("ha_user_id") val haUserId: String?,
    /**
     * HA user of the device on the hub: pending = waiting for the integration to create the user and
     * deliver its token; active = user and token stored on the hub. On the hub path active means the
     * hub holds the token for its calls of <ns>.control; the device itself holds it only when it holds
